\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces The four arms of the dose--response ladder, and the frozen predictions. The statistic each $d_2$ reads is, in order, summed pairwise Euclidean distance, distance to the client median, pairwise cosine, and coordinate ordering. \emph  {Standalone} is $d_2$'s own ASR (clean accuracy) on that attack, the C1 input, held fixed within every arm. \emph  {Measured disturbance} is the fraction of live rounds on which the rung changes that arm's decision---for \texttt  {coord\_median}, the mean fraction of \emph  {coordinates} whose median-attaining client changes---measured before the freeze on the same raw updates, with no ASR computed (\texttt  {results/dose\_disturbance.json}). Shapes and decision rules are frozen at commit \texttt  {e711a95}.}}{30}{table.caption.21}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:dose_design}{{8}{30}{The four arms of the dose--response ladder, and the frozen predictions. The statistic each $d_2$ reads is, in order, summed pairwise Euclidean distance, distance to the client median, pairwise cosine, and coordinate ordering. \emph {Standalone} is $d_2$'s own ASR (clean accuracy) on that attack, the C1 input, held fixed within every arm. \emph {Measured disturbance} is the fraction of live rounds on which the rung changes that arm's decision---for \texttt {coord\_median}, the mean fraction of \emph {coordinates} whose median-attaining client changes---measured before the freeze on the same raw updates, with no ASR computed (\texttt {results/dose\_disturbance.json}). Shapes and decision rules are frozen at commit \texttt {e711a95}}{table.caption.21}{}}
