\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The four channels, all four aggregators, under Mode~S.} Endpoint change $\kappa {=}0 \to \kappa {=}2$. \textbf  {The first column, $\Delta $~agg., is the relative displacement of the aggregate the defense \emph  {emits}}, $\|\mathrm  {agg}(T(U)) - \mathrm  {agg}(U)\|/\|\mathrm  {agg}(U)\|$---what enters training, and \textbf  {not} the value of a scoring statistic; the measured channels are aggregate displacement, decision, admission and influence. The dissociation between the \emph  {decision} channel and the \emph  {admission} channel is not a property of one aggregator: it holds for a selector, a cosine-invariant selector, a coordinate-wise order statistic and a weighted averager. The table does \textbf  {not} order the arms---$\Delta \Lambda _a$ and $\Delta $ASR disagree in rank, which is §\ref {sec:targeted}'s refutation stated in one row-pair---and it is \emph  {not} an out-of-sample test: all rows are Mode-S ladders reported elsewhere in this paper.}}{38}{table.caption.30}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:channels}{{11}{38}{\textbf {The four channels, all four aggregators, under Mode~S.} Endpoint change $\kappa {=}0 \to \kappa {=}2$. \textbf {The first column, $\Delta $~agg., is the relative displacement of the aggregate the defense \emph {emits}}, $\|\mathrm {agg}(T(U)) - \mathrm {agg}(U)\|/\|\mathrm {agg}(U)\|$---what enters training, and \textbf {not} the value of a scoring statistic; the measured channels are aggregate displacement, decision, admission and influence. The dissociation between the \emph {decision} channel and the \emph {admission} channel is not a property of one aggregator: it holds for a selector, a cosine-invariant selector, a coordinate-wise order statistic and a weighted averager. The table does \textbf {not} order the arms---$\Delta \Lambda _a$ and $\Delta $ASR disagree in rank, which is §\ref {sec:targeted}'s refutation stated in one row-pair---and it is \emph {not} an out-of-sample test: all rows are Mode-S ladders reported elsewhere in this paper}{table.caption.30}{}}
