\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The evaluated settings, plotted. No regimes, and one line, which is a measurement.} Each marker is a setting we ran, placed in the two coordinates that organize them: persistence retention $\gamma $ against the best single constituent defense's ASR, $p_{\mathrm  {eff}}$. At $\gamma {=}0$, the stateless spam game, where randomization has value (VoPD $=0.200$). At the measured FL persistence $\hat  \gamma \approx 0.66$ (the dotted line): the NC/fedavg temporal mix at ASR $0.956$, the C1-FAIL Rep$+$TM pair, and the two criterion-PASS compositions. Each point carries its own measured value as its label. \textbf  {An earlier version of this figure shaded four regime bands and drew threshold guides at $\gamma {=}0.15$, $p_{\mathrm  {eff}}{=}0.3$ and $p_{\mathrm  {eff}}{=}0.6$; none of those three numbers was measured, so all six are gone.} Five points cannot locate a boundary, and nothing here is evidence of a phase transition in $(\gamma , p_{\mathrm  {eff}})$ space.}}{41}{figure.caption.34}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:phase_boundary}{{6}{41}{\textbf {The evaluated settings, plotted. No regimes, and one line, which is a measurement.} Each marker is a setting we ran, placed in the two coordinates that organize them: persistence retention $\gamma $ against the best single constituent defense's ASR, $p_{\mathrm {eff}}$. At $\gamma {=}0$, the stateless spam game, where randomization has value (VoPD $=0.200$). At the measured FL persistence $\hat \gamma \approx 0.66$ (the dotted line): the NC/fedavg temporal mix at ASR $0.956$, the C1-FAIL Rep$+$TM pair, and the two criterion-PASS compositions. Each point carries its own measured value as its label. \textbf {An earlier version of this figure shaded four regime bands and drew threshold guides at $\gamma {=}0.15$, $p_{\mathrm {eff}}{=}0.3$ and $p_{\mathrm {eff}}{=}0.6$; none of those three numbers was measured, so all six are gone.} Five points cannot locate a boundary, and nothing here is evidence of a phase transition in $(\gamma , p_{\mathrm {eff}})$ space}{figure.caption.34}{}}
