\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Per-seed ASR(model scaling, FedAvg) vs.\ per-round adversarial participation probability $P(\geq \!1\,\text  {adv/round})$ (CIFAR-10, $4{\times }5$ game, $f=0.2$). The threshold mechanism is visible: at $N=10$ ($P=0.778$), ASR is binary (Bernoulli); at $N=20$ ($P=0.624$, $K/N$ drops), ASR clusters near zero; at $N=50,100$ ($P=0.917, 0.993$), ASR rises to near-deterministic. Diamonds show mean~$\pm $~std per scale.}}{64}{figure.caption.52}\protected@file@percent }
